# Exported Buzz agent definitions are byte-for-byte copies of what Buzz Desktop
# runs. Formatting them edits the agents' actual instructions — prettier reflows
# blockquote indentation and inserts blank lines, which changes the prompt text
# and makes `export-agents.mjs --check` report drift on every run.
buzz-agents/agents/

# The nest is byte-for-byte operational tooling for the same reason. Its guides are
# read at runtime (Janice loads JANICE_REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md every review) and its
# schema guide is the DDL source that deploy-claire-channel.sh runs through sed —
# reflowing a fenced SQL block or a table would change what actually executes.
nest/
